      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T13:58:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Typically, an adapter won\u0027t know which adapter is managing a device. (for instance, a broadcom onu may be managed by a tibit_onu adapter).     However, the adapter knows which device it controls.   For the publish scenario, the method signature should be \u0027publish_inter_adapter_message(self, device_id, msg)\u0027  and it would be up to the adapter_agent to figure out which adapter topic to send this message.",
      "revId": "f5101822e019b0abeba0bdbee099cca49f4f3898",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_500c8242",
        "filename": "voltha/core/adapter_agent.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 517,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000129
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T17:17:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that\u0027s probably a better solution. \nFor the ONU adapter that is not a problem since it can easily access it\u0027s parent device ID. For the OLT adapter however, there is currently no easy way to find out the device_id of any of the OLT\u0027s child devices.\nI am suggesting a change to the \"child_device_detected\" method in adapter_agent in order to have it return the \"device_id\" of the child device that was created. What do you think of that?",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_1093aafb",
      "revId": "f5101822e019b0abeba0bdbee099cca49f4f3898",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_b32be881",
        "filename": "voltha/core/adapter_agent.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
